      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Research in cross-cultural psychology suggests that East Asian individuals often display collectivist values, favoring harmony and group cohesion which can result in a more methodical and reflective approach to stress management in high-pressure situations. In contrast, Middle Eastern/North African cultures, with strong communal ties, may also exhibit collectivist tendencies but can also demonstrate a greater inclination toward perseverance and resilience, possibly due to historical and socio-political factors influencing their stress responses. Furthermore, some studies indicate a divergence in coping strategies, with East Asians leaning towards experiential avoidance while Middle Eastern/North Africans might prioritize seeking social support.",
